G|0|0|0|0|0|Parity ok: discrepancy (named_skeptic=1) >= reconcile (1 excerpt). Both connectives accurate/on-tension, no overclaim. Theissen, Sociology of Early Palestinian Christianity (Fortress 1978) is real; his wandering-charismatics/family-renunciation thesis genuinely rests on sayings like Luke 14:26 as evidence of the itinerant ethos later household codes ("love patriarchalism") temper — fairly represented, not strawmanned. Discrepancy pole is named_skeptic (not empty), satisfying lean=discrepancy_first. Deeper-learning verified: Haley 1874 p.286 "Kindred, how regarded: Hated. — Loved." parallel-column heading setting Luke 14:26 against Eph 5:25/33, quoting Stuart ("stronger affection... love... weaker... hatred") and Alford, confirmed verbatim via Internet Archive search-inside (scan p.304, index confirms printed p.286); gotquestions.org link verified real, on-topic, cross-refs Mark 7:9-13 and 1 Tim 5:8 as claimed.
